Conversion 5 of docs/research-notes/cumulative-coherence-rule-to-check-2026-08-21.md
— the extension the Pre-Launch Preconditions Discipline's own prose
requested for the METHODOLOGY_MISSING detector and never got.

check_preconditions_declared warns when an artifact declaring
live_llm_inference, live_llm_embedding_extraction, or hardware_smoke
lacks a preconditions_checked field. Presence-only (the field's content
is unlintable) and keyed on the explicit substrate declaration via the
shared helpers, so principle-wrapped and note-suffixed declarations are
handled and aggregation / scoring / no-LLM artifacts never draw a
category error.

Severity WARN, decided on evidence: backfill dry-run over 6,832 corpus
artifacts flags 101 (1.5%) — historical artifacts predating the
discipline (82 live_llm_inference, 17 hardware_smoke, 2 embedding).
CRITICAL would have quarantined all 101; the same precedent as
SUBSTRATE_HAS_NO_DURATION_FLOOR (720). 5 tests, including one through
the real verify_artifact entrypoint (a check nothing calls is the bug
class).

Also: check_torch_cuda.py probe timeout 15s -> 90s. Under the current
GPU A/B load the torch import alone exceeded 15s, and the guard blocked
every commit with a false 'not a CUDA build' (direct probe:
2.11.0+cu128, CUDA available). The check detects build flavor, not
speed; the raise loses no detection.

